Changelog: 22-11-2026 21:22:28

Added. Exit PCSX2 is the first button under the games table. It ends PCSX2 at once, with everything it started, and asks
nothing first. It is on only while PCSX2 runs. A game that runs ends without saving, as its tooltip says. The line under
the tabs then says "PCSX2 was ended." The app finds PCSX2's processes with core's new processes module. The wiki chapter
has a new section, Exit PCSX2.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 20:00:16

Release 1.7.1.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 15:55:10

Fixed. The app's files that had no license line have one now, the arrow of its lists among them.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 15:19:54

Fixed. The states beside the title now use two colors: green when all is well, red when not. A warning and an off state,
such as Not installed or shadNet Off, are red now. The wiki says so.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 12:25:09

Release 1.7.0.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 11:44:56

Added. The row beside the title has a new state, Steam. Its dot is green while Steam runs and is signed in, and red when
it is not, because a game in Steam starts only then. The app looks again every few seconds. The states now show their
names alone, Installed, Controller and Steam, and the dot's color shows the state. Each tooltip opens with the state in
full, such as Not installed or No controller. The wiki describes the row. test_main_window.py tests the Steam state and
follows the new order.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 12:04:44

Release 1.6.0.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 19:26:09

Release 1.5.0.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 18:49:20

Added. The window's new order (owner, 20-11-2026: shadPS4 Manager's design in every manager). The header's pills are
the PCSX2 version, PCSX2 Install, PCSX2 Uninstall and Refresh. The row under them is Games Uninstall, Available in
Steam, BIOS Uninstall and Play time. Games Uninstall is new: it is what the Remove game… button under the table did,
and that button went. The Your games box went. Under the pills are two columns: the three state lines, each name
with a colon (PCSX2:, BIOS:, Game folder:), and beside them Installed version:, the PCSX2 version in use. The tabs
are Your games, Start game, Memory cards, Settings, View logs (it was Log) and Clear logs.

Added. A check for a game that is in Steam more than once. The app says which games and how often, the game's In
Steam box says it in its tooltip, and Update Steam lights and leaves one shortcut of each, with the latest play
time; its question says how many double shortcuts go.

Fixed. The chosen row of a table is 30 % blue, with the theme's text color: filled with the header's blue, a chosen
first row could hardly be told from the header above it.

Fixed. Start game with Steam closed started Steam and never the game, while the line said "Steam starts" (seen in
shadPS4 Manager on the board, 20-11-2026). The app now starts Steam first, waits until it takes commands, then gives
it the game's address, again when the game does not come up (core's play). The line says the game runs only once
PCSX2 does, and says when Steam did not start it. While PCSX2 runs already, Start game starts no second one.

Fixed. A shortcut whose fields Steam wrote in lower case (exe, launchoptions) was not recognized as the app's, so
Update Steam added the game a second time. They are read whatever their case now.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 13:11:18

Release 1.4.0.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 03:39:29

Added. The version manager (owner, 20-11-2026: as shadPS4's own launcher has one; core's builds). The version box in
the header is a pill: its menu lists the PCSX2 builds installed and puts another in use, and Manage versions… opens
the version manager, which downloads the nightlies and the newest stable release, each with its own catalog from
GitHub, checked against the SHA-256 GitHub publishes, adds a custom AppImage, puts a build in use and deletes one.
Builds stay side by side: Install no longer deletes the others, and puts the build this version was tried with back in
use, without a download when it is still there. Uninstall removes every build. A build other than the tested one is
said to be not tried on the board.

Changelog: 19-11-2026 22:33:16

Release 1.3.1.

Changelog: 19-11-2026 22:12:37

Fixed. The message about a newer build says it comes once it has been tried on the board, not the console (owner, 19-11-2026: board everywhere).

Changelog: 18-11-2026 04:15:16

Release 1.3.0.

Changelog: 18-11-2026 02:02:00

Added. The managers' new design, as PPSSPP Manager's: Clear logs, a tab beside Log that is a button, empties the
app's log file and the Log tab and removes the older log files. Start game stands beside Your games. The six tabs
share the window's whole width and are pills as the ones above them. Play time moved from the header to the row
of action pills. Under the header's pills only the links to PCSX2's release notes and the wiki are left, in the
type of a pill's caption; the introduction went. PCSX2's state is one line. Under the games an info symbol stands
in for the line of text about Steam; Steam in its text opens Steam. The window opens 900 wide (it was 980, and
the Settings tab made it 1129 at its narrowest), and that is its narrowest: the Settings tab has two columns
in place of three and scrolls when it is higher than the window, which opens 606 high (it was 800). The BIOS line
is the dump's name alone, or Not installed.; other dumps there are named in its tooltip. PCSX2 settings,
a button left of Remove game…, opens PCSX2's own window for what the Settings tab does not set.

